<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-08-08T23:02:06+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Sat, 08 Aug 2026 23:02:06 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Florida's millions of dumped tyres are still being cleaned up 50 years later]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133054530.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Florida is set to embark on an ambitious initiative to clear millions of old tires that were dumped offshore decades ago. Initially forming an artificial reef, these tires have since led to significant damage to natural coral ecosystems. Present surveys indicate that over half a million tires still litter thousands of acres.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-dumped-millions-of-tyres-into-the-ocean-to-build-a-reef-more-than-50-years-later-it-is-still-cleaning-them-up/articleshow/133054530.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-dumped-millions-of-tyres-into-the-ocean-to-build-a-reef-more-than-50-years-later-it-is-still-cleaning-them-up/articleshow/133054530.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T20:06:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133054605,imgsize-124813.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Inside Portugal’s 19th-century goat tower, where dwarf goats climb a spiral ramp]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133056289.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/inside-portugals-19th-century-goat-tower-where-dwarf-goats-climb-a-spiral-ramp-to-a-three-storey-home/articleshow/133056289.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/inside-portugals-19th-century-goat-tower-where-dwarf-goats-climb-a-spiral-ramp-to-a-three-storey-home/articleshow/133056289.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T22:52:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133056535,imgsize-50458.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Costa Rica's tiny 'coffee frog,' a nocturnal species found living among coffee shrubs]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133055805.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A remarkable discovery in Costa Rica reveals a diminutive nocturnal frog inhabiting the coffee plantations. Measuring less than four centimeters, this unique species relies on small insects for food and foliage for protection. Essential to its lifecycle are local streams, which face risks from pesticide runoff. This finding not only emphasizes the rich biodiversity in agricultural settings but also the urgent need for conservation initiatives.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-costa-ricas-tiny-coffee-frog-a-nocturnal-species-found-living-among-coffee-shrubs/articleshow/133055805.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-costa-ricas-tiny-coffee-frog-a-nocturnal-species-found-living-among-coffee-shrubs/articleshow/133055805.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T22:17:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133055926,imgsize-1923856.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[2-year-old sister becomes perfect bone marrow match for Utah girl with aplastic anemia]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133055066.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Emma Meline, a young girl diagnosed with severe aplastic anemia right before Christmas, found hope in her little sister Lucy. At only two years old, Lucy bravely became a bone marrow donor, granting Emma the chance for a life-saving transplant. After a challenging journey, Emma celebrated her fifth birthday at home, marking a remarkable recovery. This profound experience deepened the unbreakable bond between the two sisters.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/utah-girl-emma-meline-was-diagnosed-with-severe-aplastic-anemia-days-before-christmas-her-2-year-old-sister-became-her-perfect-bone-marrow-match/articleshow/133055066.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/utah-girl-emma-meline-was-diagnosed-with-severe-aplastic-anemia-days-before-christmas-her-2-year-old-sister-became-her-perfect-bone-marrow-match/articleshow/133055066.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T21:00:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmln